@startuml j1-first-open
!include c4-sequence.iuml
title J1 First open and the sample shop
actor "Owner" as O <<person>>
box "Hisaab in the browser"
participant "Home screen\n(index.html, app.js)" as H <<container>>
participant "Layout\n(compact.js)" as L <<component>>
database "Browser storage\n(localStorage)" as S <<store>>
participant "Service worker\n(sw.js)" as W <<container>>
end box
== First open ==
O -> H : open the live link
H -> S : read the saved theme, language and shop
S --> H : nothing saved yet: an empty shop, "My shop"
H --> O : "No customers yet." with the buttons\n"Add your first customer" and "Load sample shop"
H -> W : register the service worker once the page has loaded
note over S : no account and no server:\nthe shop lives only in this browser
== The sample shop ==
O -> H : tap "Load sample shop"
H -> H : fetch sample-data.json from the site itself\n(sample.js is the copy used if that fails)
H -> S : save "Lakshmi Provision Store (fictional)"
H --> O : "Loaded Lakshmi Provision Store (fictional):\n8 customers, 38 entries." and "Shop loaded." with "Undo"
L --> O : "Total outstanding" with the strip "Customers", "Overdue",\n"Collected, last 30 days"; the customer list;\nthe quick entry pill with "+" at the bottom
note right of L : balance = all credit minus all payments,\nworked out each time, never stored
opt the screen is 1200 px wide or more
  L --> O : on a screen 1200 px wide or more: a right panel with\n"Record an entry", "Overdue" and "Recent entries"
end
opt the owner wants the full overview
  O -> L : tap "…" in the strip
  L --> O : the full overview: "Owes the most", "Collected, last 30 days",\n"Given on credit, last 30 days", "Longest without paying"
end
@enduml
